module serialDilutionDetection
module proteinDigestionDetection

manifest AnalyteFluorescein
manifest InternalStandardRhodamine123
manifest Diluent
manifest AF_BSA
manifest PepsinSolution
manifest TrypsinSolution
manifest PluronicF68

// ============================================================
// Multilayer Hybrid Microfluidics: A Digital-to-Channel
// Interface for Sample Processing and Separations
// Watson, Jebrail, Wheeler - Anal. Chem. 2010, 82, 6680-6686
// DOI: 10.1021/ac101379g
//
// This file encodes two on-chip protocols demonstrated on a
// two-plate DMF multilayer hybrid device (glass substrate,
// 13 driving electrodes 2.2x2.2 mm, 3 reservoir electrodes
// 3x3 mm or 5x5 mm). The DMF layer (substrates 1+2) sits
// atop a microchannel network (substrate 3, 100 um wide x
// 20 um deep). Droplets processed on the top DMF layer are
// delivered through a vertical digital-channel interface
// (drilled hole, 2 mm dia.) into microchannels below for
// capillary electrophoresis (CE) analysis with LIF detection
// (488 nm excitation, 536/40 nm emission).
//
// AC actuation: 20 kHz, 100-200 Vrms.
// Spacer gap: 280 um (4x double-sided tape).
// Unit droplet: ~3 uL (fills the 2 mm dia. x 1 mm deep hole).
// Separation buffer: 20 mM borate pH 9.0 (dilution) or
//                   100 mM borate pH 9.0 (enzyme digests).
// Pluronic F-68 added to all protein-containing droplets at
// 0.1% wt to minimise surface adsorption.
//
// PROTOCOL 1: On-Chip Serial Dilution Calibration Curve
//   Stock droplet: 1 uM fluorescein + 1 uM rhodamine 123 in
//   20 mM borate pH 9.0. Diluent: 1 uM rhodamine 123 in
//   20 mM borate pH 9.0 (internal standard maintained constant).
//   Dilution 1: stock + diluent -> mix (circular, ~10 s) ->
//     split into two equal subdroplets (2x dilution, ~0.5 uM Flu).
//     Daughter A: drive to interface for CE-LIF analysis.
//     Daughter B: store on array for second dilution step.
//   Dilution 2: stored Daughter B + fresh diluent -> mix ->
//     split. Daughter C: drive to interface for CE-LIF analysis.
//   Precision: RSD = 2.9% (stock), 3.7% (1st), 7.4% (2nd).
//   Efficiency: 1.1e6 plates/m for rhodamine 123.
//   R^2 = 0.9937 across five replicates.
//
// PROTOCOL 2: Multistep Enzymatic Protein Digestion
//   Model protein: AF-BSA (Alexa Fluor 488 labeled bovine serum
//   albumin, 20 ug/mL in DI water + 0.1% F-68).
//   Pepsin: 1 mg/mL in 1 mM acetate buffer + 0.1% F-68, pH 4.5.
//     Cleaves at aromatic residues (Phe, Tyr, Trp). 30 min.
//   Trypsin: 1 mg/mL in 50 mM borate buffer + 0.1% F-68, pH 9.0.
//     Cleaves at basic residues (Lys, Arg). 30 min.
//   Sequential digest: AF-BSA -> pepsin (30 min) -> split ->
//     subdroplet to interface for CE; stored half merged with
//     trypsin (30 min) -> deliver to interface.
//   Incubation: device stored in humidified Petri dish (water-
//     saturated wipe) during 30 min steps to limit evaporation.
//   Total process time: ~2 h including both incubation steps.
//
// NOTE ON split ABSTRACTION: BioScript does not have a native
//   `split` statement. Physical droplet splitting on the array
//   (two daughter droplets of equal volume) is abstracted here
//   as a `mix` step with a secondary dispense that represents
//   the stored subdroplet being retained on the array. The
//   subdroplet driven to the digital-channel interface is the
//   primary product variable at each split point. This is a
//   compiler-compatible representation; the actual split is
//   performed by reversing the electrode actuation sequence
//   while the droplet straddles two electrodes.
//
// NOTE ON DURATION TOKENS: BioScript accepts s and m only.
//   30 min incubations are encoded as 30m.
//   Circular mixing for several seconds is encoded as 10s.
//
// NOTE ON dispense RESTRICTION: Only manifest-declared reagents
//   may appear as the source in a dispense statement.
//   The digital-channel interface transfer (droplet driven to
//   the microchannel inlet) is modelled via detect statements
//   using the serialDilutionDetection or proteinDigestionDetection
//   modules, which abstract CE-LIF analysis in the channel layer.
//
// NOTE ON VARIABLE REASSIGNMENT: BioScript does not permit
//   reassignment of a variable once bound. All intermediate
//   droplets (post-mix, post-detect) use unique identifiers.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main             -- entry: serial dilution protocol
//                           (dispense, dilution 1, dilution 2)
//                           followed by protein digestion protocol
//   BB2  dilutionPass     -- dilutionSignal > 0: valid CE peaks
//                           detected; dispose analysed droplets
//   BB3  dilutionFail     -- dilutionSignal <= 0: no signal; drain
//   BB4  dilutionJoin     -- join: protein digestion branch begins
//   BB5  digestionPass    -- digestionSignal > 0: valid digest
//                           peaks; dispose all digestion droplets
//   BB6  digestionFail    -- digestionSignal <= 0: no peaks; drain
//   BB7  finalCleanup     -- terminal: dispose QC signals; end
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 1: On-Chip Serial Dilution Calibration Curve
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Dispense stock droplet.
//   Reservoir contains 1 uM fluorescein + 1 uM rhodamine 123
//   in 20 mM borate buffer pH 9.0. Unit droplet: ~3 uL.
//   Actuation: 20 kHz, 100-200 Vrms, two-plate format.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

stockDroplet = dispense 1 units of AnalyteFluorescein

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Dispense first diluent droplet.
//   Reservoir contains 1 uM rhodamine 123 (internal standard)
//   in 20 mM borate buffer pH 9.0. No fluorescein present.
//   Merging with stock will halve fluorescein concentration
//   while maintaining constant internal standard.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

diluent1 = dispense 1 units of Diluent

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Merge stock and first diluent droplet.
//   Merged droplet (~0.5 uM fluorescein, ~1 uM rhodamine 123).
//   Circular mixing pattern (several electrode actuations)
//   ensures thorough homogenisation before splitting.
//   Mix duration: ~10 s on-chip (paper: "several seconds").
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mergedDrop1 = mix stockDroplet with diluent1 for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Dilution 1 - split merged droplet.
//   Physical split: reverse electrode sequence while droplet
//   straddles two driving electrodes; two ~1.5 uL subdroplets
//   result. Daughter A is driven to the digital-channel
//   interface. Daughter B is stored on the array.
//   Abstracted here: the split product variable represents
//   the daughter subdroplet A (~0.5 uM Flu, ~1 uM Rho).
//   A second dispense of Diluent abstracts the stored
//   Daughter B remaining on the electrode array.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Daughter A: subdroplet analysed by CE-LIF at channel interface.
dilution1Analysed = mix mergedDrop1 with diluent1 for 2s

// Daughter B: stored on array for second dilution.
// NOTE: A fresh diluent dispense models the stored half-droplet
// equivalent volume; it is the logical placeholder for the
// retained subdroplet that will be further diluted in STEP 6.
storedDrop1 = dispense 1 units of Diluent

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: CE-LIF detection at digital-channel interface.
//   Daughter A is actuated to the interface electrode (2.2x2.2
//   mm, overlapping the 2 mm dia. drilled hole by ~1 mm).
//   The droplet spontaneously wets and settles into the hole.
//   DC voltages (LabSmith sequencer) drive sample through the
//   cross injector into the 3 cm separation channel.
//   Loading: S=900V, SW=0V, B=650V, BW=850V.
//   Injection: S=500V, SW=500V, B=1000V, BW=0V.
//   LIF detection at 3 cm downstream (488 nm, 20 mW argon ion,
//   60x objective, 536/40 nm BP filter, PMT readout).
//   Peak area (AA) relative to IS (AIS) recorded.
//   The sample waste channel removes the previous analysed
//   sample by suction before the next injection.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dilutionSignal1 = detect serialDilutionDetection on dilution1Analysed for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Dilution 2 - merge stored Daughter B with fresh diluent.
//   Stored subdroplet (Daughter B, ~0.5 uM Flu) merged with a
//   second unit diluent droplet. Result: ~0.25 uM fluorescein,
//   ~1 uM rhodamine 123 (4x dilution relative to original stock).
//   Mixed circularly for ~10 s to homogenise.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

diluent2 = dispense 1 units of Diluent
mergedDrop2 = mix storedDrop1 with diluent2 for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Dilution 2 - split and deliver second daughter droplet.
//   Daughter C (~0.25 uM Flu, ~1 uM Rho) driven to interface.
//   Previous sample removed from channel by suction before
//   this injection, without removing the DMF top-plate.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dilution2Analysed = mix mergedDrop2 with diluent2 for 2s

// CE-LIF detection for the second dilution point.
dilutionSignal2 = detect serialDilutionDetection on dilution2Analysed for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Serial dilution QC gate
// Keyed on dilutionSignal1 (undiluted first daughter;
// highest fluorescein signal, most reliable peak detection).
// Pass (BB2): dilutionSignal1 > 0 -> valid electropherogram
//             peaks resolved; baseline separation confirmed;
//             dispose analysed droplets.
// Fail (BB3): dilutionSignal1 <= 0 -> no peaks (interface
//             transfer failed or separation column clogged);
//             drain and abort calibration run.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (dilutionJoin).
// ============================================================

if (dilutionSignal1 > 0) {
    dispose dilution1Analysed
    dispose dilution2Analysed
} else {
    drain dilution1Analysed
    drain dilution2Analysed
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: dilutionJoin
// Dispose serial dilution QC signal droplets.
// Control falls into protein digestion branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose dilutionSignal1
dispose dilutionSignal2

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 2: Multistep Enzymatic Protein Digestion (AF-BSA)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Dispense AF-BSA droplet.
//   20 ug/mL AF-BSA in DI water + 0.1% Pluronic F-68.
//   Unit droplet: ~3 uL. F-68 additive minimises protein
//   adsorption to device surfaces (Parylene-C / Teflon-AF).
//   Device uses 100 mM borate buffer pH 9.0 as channel fill
//   for enzymatic digest runs (higher ionic strength for
//   protein fragment separation).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

afbsaDroplet = dispense 1 units of AF_BSA

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Dispense pepsin droplet.
//   1 mg/mL pepsin in 1 mM acetate buffer + 0.1% F-68, pH 4.5.
//   Pepsin cleaves at aromatic residues (Phe, Tyr, Trp),
//   generating multiply charged peptide fragments.
//   Unit droplet: ~3 uL.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pepsinDroplet = dispense 1 units of PepsinSolution

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Merge AF-BSA with pepsin and incubate.
//   Merged droplet (~6 uL, 2 units) contains AF-BSA + pepsin
//   in equal volumes. Mixed briefly on the DMF array to ensure
//   homogeneous enzyme-substrate contact before incubation.
//   Device transferred to humidified chamber (Petri dish with
//   water-saturated wipe) to limit droplet evaporation during
//   the 30 min incubation at room temperature.
//   After incubation, AF-BSA peak at t=58 s is absent from
//   CE electropherogram, confirming complete digestion.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pepsinReaction = mix afbsaDroplet with pepsinDroplet for 5s
heat pepsinReaction at 25c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: Split pepsin digest; deliver first subdroplet to
//   digital-channel interface for CE-LIF analysis.
//   Daughter D: driven to interface (pepsin-only digest).
//   Daughter E: stored on array for sequential trypsin step.
//   CE electropherogram shows multiple peaks eluting at a range
//   of times relative to the AF-BSA reactant peak (multiply
//   charged aromatic peptides generated by pepsin cleavage).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Daughter D: analysed by CE-LIF (pepsin digest only).
pepsinAnalysed = mix pepsinReaction with pepsinDroplet for 2s

// Daughter E: stored subdroplet (logical placeholder).
storedPepsinDrop = dispense 1 units of AF_BSA

// CE-LIF detection for pepsin-only digest.
digestionSignalPepsin = detect proteinDigestionDetection on pepsinAnalysed for 60s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 12: Dispense trypsin droplet.
//   1 mg/mL trypsin in 50 mM borate buffer + 0.1% F-68, pH 9.0.
//   Trypsin cleaves at basic residues (Lys, Arg), reducing the
//   multiply charged peptides from pepsin into smaller fragments
//   that elute closer together in the CE separation.
//   Unit droplet: ~3 uL.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

trypsinDroplet = dispense 1 units of TrypsinSolution

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 13: Merge stored pepsin digest half with trypsin and
//   incubate for a second 30 min digestion at room temperature.
//   Sequential two-enzyme digest: pepsin then trypsin generates
//   singly charged peptides observable in the top CE trace
//   (Fig 6, paper). Device returned to humidified chamber.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

trypsinReaction = mix storedPepsinDrop with trypsinDroplet for 5s
heat trypsinReaction at 25c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 14: Deliver sequential digest subdroplet to interface.
//   Full pepsin+trypsin digest driven to digital-channel
//   interface for CE-LIF analysis. Previous sample removed
//   from channel by suction (fine needle + vacuum flask)
//   without removing the DMF top-plate between injections.
//   CE electropherogram shows new series of peaks (peptides
//   eluting closer together vs pepsin-only digest).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sequentialDigestAnalysed = mix trypsinReaction with trypsinDroplet for 2s

// CE-LIF detection for sequential pepsin + trypsin digest.
digestionSignalSeq = detect proteinDigestionDetection on sequentialDigestAnalysed for 60s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Protein digestion QC gate
// Keyed on pepsin-only digestion signal (Step 11 detection;
// most diagnostic -- loss of intact AF-BSA peak at t=58 s
// confirms complete first-stage digestion).
// Pass (BB5): digestionSignalPepsin > 0 -> valid CE peaks
//             detected (peptide fragments resolved); dispose
//             all digestion droplets.
// Fail (BB6): digestionSignalPepsin <= 0 -> no signal (enzyme
//             inactive, transfer failed, or column blocked);
//             drain all digestion droplets.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (digestionSignalPepsin > 0) {
    dispose pepsinAnalysed
    dispose sequentialDigestAnalysed
} else {
    drain pepsinAnalysed
    drain sequentialDigestAnalysed
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all QC signal droplets. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose digestionSignalPepsin
dispose digestionSignalSeq

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
